## 17. Definition of done

A feature is not complete simply because its screen exists.

A feature is considered implemented only when:
- Its UI exists.
- Its state transitions and business logic work.
- Required backend operations exist.
- Access control is enforced.
- Errors and unavailable states are handled.
- Relevant tests exist.
- Its setup requirements are documented.
- The interface reports actual state rather than fabricated success.

Before calling the project ready, verify that:
- All 23 feature areas have an explicit implementation status.
- SOS works without AI.
- Last-known coordinates preserve their original timestamp and accuracy.
- A failed transmission is never shown as delivered.
- Duplicate retries do not create duplicate emergency sessions.
- Private evidence and location records cannot be accessed by unauthorized users.
- Test alerts cannot reach real emergency services.
- AI outputs do not invent source references.
- Users can review and control their data.
- Essential screens support English, Hindi, and Marathi.
- Critical failure states are understandable and accessible.
- Build and test results are reported honestly.
- Unconfigured integrations are explicitly listed.
- No secrets or sensitive sample data are committed.
- Production-readiness claims match actual verification.

